# UI KISS — sleek and simple

Keep the CPU window **sleek**, **simple**, and **KISS**. Do not add chrome that fights the layout or repeats a cue that is already visible.

## Do

- Prefer **one** clear signal (card wash, sparkline tint, icon status).
- Keep sparklines aligned under their gauges (CPU · GPU · FREQ · TEMP).
- Prefer in-place washes (`.is-hot` on the card or chart) over extra bars or chips.
- When in doubt, leave the control out.

## Do not

- Insert **Hot · …** attention bars that sit in the sparkline flex row or under the power strip (they shift layout and duplicate the card wash).
- Add full-width “Hot” banners, redundant summary chips, or second labels for the same metric.
- Trade alignment for “operator parity” glances on the main metrics surface.

## Hot metrics

Ring cards and matching history charts may use `.is-hot` / `.is-fair` washes. That is enough.

Do **not** bring back:

- `#history-hot-attention-glance` (e.g. “Hot · GPU”)
- `#power-strip-hot-attention-glance` (e.g. “Hot · Up”)

Process-list Hot filter chips and section glances (Top Processes) are separate — keep those if they help filtering.

## Examples

```text
❌ Hot · GPU chip beside sparklines (pushes TEMP to the next row)
❌ Full-width Hot · Up under the battery strip
✅ GPU metric card amber wash only
✅ History chart `.is-hot` wash only
```
